---
// PROTOTYPE (plank/docs#22): the doc pages' display menu. The User asked on 2026-09-13 for the theme and
// the reduced-motion setting in one dropdown, each under its own sub-heading, opened by plank.co's
// accessibility icon. It replaces plank/docs#19's one-click theme toggle on doc pages.
// It overrides Starlight's ThemeSelect, so it sits in the header on desktop and in the menu drawer's
// footer on phones, where Starlight puts its select.
// - Theme: Light or Dark, stored under Starlight's own key, `starlight-theme`, so Starlight's inline
//   script still sets it before first paint. Until a reader picks, the system theme is followed.
// - Motion: plank.co's switch. It can only reduce: when the OS asks for reduced motion, it shows on, locked.
import { Icon } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';

const id = `pm-${Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 8)}`;
---

<div class="pm">
	<button type="button" class="pm-trigger" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls={id} aria-label="Theme and motion">
		<svg viewBox="0 0 34 32" aria-hidden="true">
			<path
				fill="currentColor"
